coder › Done. Implemented the token bucket and added tests on branch `work/main`.

## What changed

**`src/limiter.ts`** — implemented `RateLimiter` using lazy refill-on-read:
- Starts full: `tokens` initialized to `capacity`, `lastRefill` to `this.now()`.
- `tryTake(n)`: refuses immediately when `n > capacity` (so even a full bucket can't hand out more than capacity); otherwise refills to the current time, then takes `n` if `this.tokens >= n` — otherwise returns `false` and leaves the bucket untouched.
- `available`: refills to `this.now()` and returns the bucket contents, which can be fractional (e.g. 250 ms at 1 token/s yields 0.25).
- The private `refill()` adds `elapsedMs / 1000 * refillPerSecond` and caps with `Math.min(capacity, …)`, so the bucket never exceeds capacity. It also ignores backwards clock moves (`now <= lastRefill`).

**`src/limiter.test.ts`** — kept the original "starts full" test and added: refuses to take more than capacity (takes nothing), takes nothing when not enough are available, continuous refill over time, fractional `available`, and never refilling beyond capacity.

