## Notes / decisions not spelled out in the plan

- Refill is computed lazily on each `tryTake`/`available` call rather than on a timer, which is the standard way to honor an injectable `now` — nothing needs a background tick.
- A backwards clock jump is treated as "no refill yet" (guard `now <= lastRefill`), and `lastRefill` is only advanced when a refill actually happens.
- `n <= 0` wasn't specified; I left it with the obvious arithmetic behavior (`n = 0` succeeds taking nothing) rather than adding unspecified rules. One test I wrote initially was wrong — I had moved the clock backwards inside a "continuous refill" test — and I fixed it to use a monotonic timeline before committing.

